  <prompt>Owner UAT round 9 (2026-10-07), item 2. Record: `notes/042-uat-round9-2026-10-07.md`.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer on the Office add-in (React 19, Fluent UI v9).</role>

  <goal>Nothing in the toolbar overlaps at any pane width: when the row is too narrow Expand moves into "⋮" and then the tabs go icon-only; Expand/Collapse use a pane icon.</goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner item 2">No overlap in Word at default width; Expand stays reachable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-11 / ADR-021">Icon-only tabs keep their accessible names and tooltips; Fluent v9 only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests for each fit level and the step back up; suite gated.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Wide: labelled tabs and an inline Expand button.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Narrow: Expand is a "⋮" menu item that works; tabs icon-only with names.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Widened again: back to labelled tabs and the inline button, without flicker.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: full jest green; lint 0; typecheck 0 production.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Measure overflow in a hook with hysteresis; render the levels in the toolbar.</step>
    <step>Pane icons for Expand/Collapse.</step>
    <step>Tests; gates; notes; status.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>The toolbar (tasks 103/106) and Find's ResizeObserver use.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — the existing toolbar measures itself; one small hook, used only here.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Owner UAT round 9: the Expand button covers the last tab in Word at default width.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

